      "slice": "ReleaseTableHold",
      "description": "Polls HeldReservations for holds that have outlived their reservation window - the same wall-clock derivation NoShowsDue already does from date and startTime - and issues ReleaseTableHold for each with reason 'The hold outlived its reservation window'. This is the only release trigger the processor evaluates on its own. The blacklist and upfront-payment checks named in the reason field are staff decisions made outside this system: there is no blacklist and no payment-validation data anywhere in the model, so the processor never derives those reasons - it only ever passes them through when a caller supplies one. The command accepts any reason string, which is why its specifications still cover all three.",
      "context": "INTERNAL",
      "elementContext": "INTERNAL",
      "listElement": false,
      "todoList": false,
      "createsAggregate": false,
      "elementCopy": false,
      "sketched": false,
      "comments": []
    }
  ],
